{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: exact group B head da8b4e5a2808d40179d1b27cc449e1ec06ab3a8d on planner/docs-paths-b1-20261110, all 13 artifacts, for request 16e74c59 of documentation request 044311b0 under promise c0ab97b2 and review request e76fb114. The structure is sound and most statements hold. Five statements contradict the source, and two of them send a reader down a path that fails without saying so.\n\nRequired changes:\n\n1. `docs/operate-a-service.md`: the working directory goes wrong. Step 3 of \"Read health\" runs `cd apps/room` (line 47) and never returns to the repository root. The deploy section then runs `git diff ORIG_HEAD HEAD -- apps/room/wrangler.jsonc` (line 90). Git reads that path relative to the current directory, so from `apps/room` the diff prints nothing and hides a new Durable Object migration, which is the case the next step guards against. The later `cd apps/room` lines (129, 207, 232) fail when the reader is already there. End each block that enters `apps/room` with `cd ../..`, as `docs/self-host.md` does, or give the `git diff` a `-C` to the root.\n\n2. `apps/room/docs/page.md:104-105` says the page \"does not update on its own\" and tells the reader to reload. The page does update. `observeView` in `apps/room/page/src/main.ts:209-216` binds each issue, change, rules and list screen (lines 1118, 1176, 1201, 1235) to its scope and redraws when the head changes. `page-observation.ts` follows the stream and falls back to polling. State that the screens follow the room and fall back to polling when the stream is unavailable. The same stale sentence sits in the moved reference at `apps/room/page/README.md:225-226`. It was already wrong on main, and correcting it there too keeps the two pages in agreement.\n\n3. `docs/connect-an-ai-app.md:98-101` offers the `join` tool as an alternative \"with the link\", and lines 39-43 offer an `artroom-invite:` link or an `artroom-device-key:` link. The MCP `join` tool accepts only an invitation: `packages/mcp/src/service.ts:1494` parses with `invitationOf` and refuses anything else with `declared: \"artroom-invite:...\"`. Limit the alternative to an invitation link.\n\n4. `apps/room/docs/page.md:63-64` says each change in the list shows **Waiting for review**, **Needs review**, **Awaiting confirmation** or **Merged**. The **Changes** list shows **Closed**, **Merged** or the lane's raw state (`apps/room/page/src/view.ts:99`). The four labels come from `changeCondition` (`view.ts:157-170`) and appear on the change page. Move the sentence to the change page, or name the labels the list shows.\n\n5. `apps/room/docs/landing.md:55` says only the change's author can link it to an issue. That holds for `--closes`, which signs `link-own`. `change.json`, `change3.json` and `change-evidence4.json` in `apps/room/lanes/definitions/` also declare `link-any`, which an admin or maintainer holds through `change.edit-any`. Say that `--closes` links as the author.\n\nSmaller corrections, which the next head can take with the five above:\n\n- `docs/operate-a-service.md:64-66` points to self-host step 3 for the `METRICS` binding, and that step lets the operator choose any dataset name. `scripts/deploy-check.mjs:29` reads only `artroom_metrics_v1`. Name that dataset.\n- `docs/operate-a-service.md:172` says the command prints the read token's handle. It prints `Read token: \u003cscope\u003e:\u003cseq\u003e, until \u003cends\u003e.` (`packages/cli/src/command-repository.ts:193`), the position of the act. Lines 183-184 quote the archive fetch line without its second sentence, \"Verify the expected journal set offline before accepting the archive.\"\n- `apps/room/docs/reviewing.md:42-43` and `page.md:98-99` say a version with several files has no **Review change** task. That holds for the task button, but **Advanced** still offers the `review-verdict` form with the heading **Review change** and its `manifest` filled in (`main.ts:694-697`, `1126`; `actions.ts:39`, `79-84`). Mention that form, or say the guided task is absent.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- Scope. Main ca6afe2b is an ancestor, the head is pushed, and the planner's worktree is clean at the head. Against main, the head changes exactly the 13 paths that its 13 artifacts cover, all Markdown. The commit-message check passes: 1 checked, 0 flagged.\n- The links. On my own extracted copy of the head, `scripts/check-doc-links.mjs` checks 1,149 local links and finds none broken. All 39 pages under `docs/` are reachable from `docs/README.md` through relative links.\n- The wording. No added line names a workroom actor or ruling. The word \"checker\" appears only as the room role.\n- The move. `apps/room/page/README.md` holds the old `apps/room/docs/page.md` body unchanged, under a new title and a three-line introduction. Its one relative link still resolves.\n- The rest. I checked about 195 other statements against the source, and they hold. These include every `dap` command, flag and quoted output line in the guides, the bold labels, the refusal names, the role defaults, and the named statements that something does not exist. No registry publishes `dap`. No hosted Claude or ChatGPT run is recorded. The public demo services leave `MCP_ENABLED` unset. A migration cannot be rolled back. The archive runs only for the demo room on dap-grow. No backup command exists, and `scripts/usage-report.mjs` refuses an unlisted Worker with `worker-unknown`.\n\nArchitecture: sound. Six reader doors in one index, with how-to guides that put the browser first and the command second, give each audience one start. Moving the contributor reference beside the page source keeps reader pages free of build detail.\n\nSecurity: the operator guide's `git diff` is the one finding with an operational consequence. A reader who follows it from `apps/room` sees no migration and can deploy a one-way Durable Object migration without the check that step 4 asks for. The rest of the change touches documents only and adds no credential, route or setting.\n\nSimplification: no further change. The new pages repeat no reference material and link to it instead.\n\nThis verdict authorizes no landing. A new head with the five required changes can come back for review.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1dbc6d9dc770a981a6cbdb5f584ac65caf435ff9","binding":"assigned","head":"da8b4e5a2808d40179d1b27cc449e1ec06ab3a8d","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7851dc24977026e5afbffe5e7e2e1e3e9b4c1947\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c0ab97b294418f990d115e7125a9d5677a3af3dd\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:88e648ea97eebca5fde085494aa37abcc5f2ece6","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}